  .call_async
    calls perform_later on the proxy class with context
    with delayed execution
      calls set(wait:) and perform_later when _async contains wait option
      calls set(wait_until:) and perform_later when _async contains wait_until option
      calls perform_later when _async is not a hash
      calls perform_later when _async is an empty hash
  behaves like async adapter per-class exception reporting
    per-class async_exception_reporting override
      when action has per-class override :every_attempt
        triggers on_exception on every attempt (respects per-class override)
      when action has per-class override :only_exhausted
        does not trigger on_exception on intermediate attempts (respects per-class override)
      when action has no per-class override
        falls back to global config behavior
  Rails version validation
    when after_discard is available (Rails 7.1+)
      allows :only_exhausted mode
      allows :first_and_exhausted mode
    when after_discard is not available (Rails < 7.1)
      allows :every_attempt mode
      raises error for :first_and_exhausted mode
      raises error for :only_exhausted mode

